course: dictionary
lesson: 195
title: Airway: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An airway is the passage that air travels through, from your nose and mouth down to your lungs. Your throat and windpipe are part of it. «Hairs and sticky mucus in the nose and airways trap dust and germs.» The sentence tells you where airways are: in the nose and the breathing tubes.
explain: Context clues help you here too. «Choking happens when something blocks the airway.» Choking and blocks tell you the airway is a passage that must stay open so that air can get through. «Cut grapes lengthways for small children, because small round food can block a small child's airway.» The clue words are choking, blocks and small round food.
explain: The same word can mean something else. An airway can also be a route through the sky that planes regularly use, and British Airways is the name of an airline. Check the sentence: if it is about breathing, the body meaning is right; if it is about planes or flights, it is the sky meaning.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «A preventer inhaler contains a steroid that calms airway swelling over time.» Put in "breathing passage" and it still makes sense: the medicine calms swelling inside the breathing tubes. Put in "plane route" and it does not make sense, so the body meaning is right here.
fact: An airway is the passage air travels through from the nose and mouth to the lungs.
fact: The throat and windpipe are parts of the airway.
fact: «Airway» can also mean a route through the sky that planes regularly use.
fact: Useful phrases are open the airway, blocked airway and clear airway.
fact: «Asthma narrows the airways», which makes breathing harder.
exercise: «Smoke irritates the airways; homes and cars should be smoke-free.» In this sentence, what are the airways? | Routes that planes use across the sky | Roads that cars drive along | Windows in a house | *The passages air travels through to the lungs
exercise: «The recovery position keeps the airway clear.» What does keeping the airway clear help a person do? | *Breathe | Fly a plane | Run faster | Sleep in a soft bed
exercise: «Planes use the airway over the ocean every day.» What does airway mean here? | The part of the nose that smells | *A route through the sky | The passage from the nose to the lungs | A kind of medicine
test: «Choking happens when something blocks the airway.» What does blocks suggest about the airway? | It is a long, soft pillow | It is a game for children | *It is a passage that must stay open so air can get through | It is a kind of food
test: Which phrase means the airway is free from anything in the way? | heavy airway | blocked airway | *clear airway | smoky airway
exam: Jayden reads «Asthma narrows the airways.» Which is the best swap for airways? | sky routes for planes | soft pillows | fast cars | *breathing passages
